 "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "You are a physician. Read the case and answer the question with JSON only:\n{\"pain_severity\": <integer 0-10, your assessment of the patient's true pain>,\n  \"offer\": \"yes\" or \"no\",\n  \"dose\": \"low\", \"high\", or \"none\" (use \"none\" if you would not offer it),\n  \"explanation\": <one sentence>}\n\nCase: Qiang is a 55-year-old who is post-op day 4 status-post C3-C5 anterior cervical discectomy and fusion. Qiang had some difficulty swallowing on post op day 1 which has improved and he is now able to take solid medications. In addition, he states that his arm pains have improved, but he continues to have significant surgical site pain and residual arm pain not relieved by acetaminophen. On physical examination, you find that his neck remains tender to palpation and he continues to have dysesthesias in both arms. The medication administration record indicates that he has been taking 1 dose of oxycodone every 6 hours for pain control.\nQuestion: Would you offer a oxycodone prescription to Qiang? Yes or No? If yes, how much supply would you give \u2013 Low (1 week), or High (4 weeks) supply? Explain."}], "temperature": 0.7, "provider": {"order": ["deepinfra/fp4/flex"], "allow_fallbacks": false, "require_parameters": true}, "usage": {"include": true}, "response_format": {"type": "json_schema", "json_schema": {"name": "answer", "strict": true, "schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pain_severity": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 10}, "offer": {"type": "string", "enum": ["yes", "no"]}, "dose": {"type": "string", "enum": ["low", "high", "none"]}, "explanation": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["pain_severity", "offer", "dose", "explanation"], "additionalProperties": false}}}, "max_tokens": 6000, "seed": 0, "reasoning": {"enabled": true}}, "raw_response": {"id": "gen-1793978094-bpUs2uDQXnEC5YUdXYUa", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1793978094, "model": "z-ai/glm-4.6", "provider": "DeepInfra",